========================
Rabin Karp Algorithm
========================

Think of this as a sliding window with an anchor point in the haystack.

ph = hash(needle, 0, m - 1);

mh = hash(haystack, 0, m - 1);

if (ph == mh) do strstr

j = 0;
for (j = 0, i = m; i < n; ++i, ++j) {
    mh /= prime(haystack[j]);
    mh *= prime(haystack[i]);

    if (ph == mh) do strstr
}

